WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:08.980
AI can accelerate attack surface documentation by extracting, organizing, normalizing, and summarizing information from authorized source material.

2
00:00:09.080 --> 00:00:18.200
It can help turn scattered evidence into component tables, interface inventories, data flow summaries, assumption lists, and open questions.

3
00:00:18.300 --> 00:00:24.300
That acceleration is valuable because manual documentation work is often slow and easy to postpone.

4
00:00:24.580 --> 00:00:27.700
The quality of the workflow depends on evidence.

5
00:00:27.800 --> 00:00:33.560
Source material should be identified, current enough for the task, and handled within approved boundaries.

6
00:00:33.660 --> 00:00:46.220
AI output should preserve provenance so reviewers can trace claims back to diagrams, repositories, inventories, manifests, tickets, scans, logs, or owner confirmation.

7
00:00:46.320 --> 00:00:50.240
Without provenance, the document becomes hard to trust.

8
00:00:50.520 --> 00:00:54.760
Strong workflows identify uncertainty instead of hiding it.

9
00:00:54.860 --> 00:01:03.820
Missing owners, unclear flows, unverified assumptions, inconsistent names, and contradictory sources should become visible review items.

10
00:01:03.920 --> 00:01:10.640
AI should ask clarifying questions and create open issues rather than inventing confident answers.

11
00:01:10.740 --> 00:01:15.540
A document that shows gaps is often more useful than one that pretends to be complete.

12
00:01:15.820 --> 00:01:18.140
Human validation is essential.

13
00:01:18.240 --> 00:01:26.880
Developers, architects, security teams, service owners, auditors, and incident responders each see different parts of the system.

14
00:01:26.980 --> 00:01:31.140
Their review turns a generated draft into practical documentation.

15
00:01:31.240 --> 00:01:40.760
Continuous maintenance keeps that documentation aligned as APIs, identities, cloud resources, dependencies, and data flows change.

16
00:01:41.040 --> 00:01:44.800
The goal is not to create polished diagrams that look complete.

17
00:01:44.900 --> 00:01:51.620
The goal is defensible, evidence-backed documentation that helps teams understand and reduce risk.

18
00:01:51.720 --> 00:02:00.680
Used well, AI becomes a documentation accelerator, while humans remain responsible for scope, validation, decisions, and maintenance.
